    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0634" n="540" xml:id="pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.12155/421: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-20T18:00:00-04:00">May 20, 1930—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>134. Your 93, May 17, noon.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d520-f1"/> In order that we may
                    make the necessary arrangements it is essential that we be informed earliest
                    moment possible whether Mexican Government is agreeable to the initiation of
                    negotiations in Mexico City some time early in July. As stated in the
                    Department’s 127<anchor n="52" xml:id="d520-f2"/> Department proposes to
                    instruct Lawson to be in Mexico City for that purpose. We also hope that Mexican
                    Boundary Commissioner will likewise be present for the discussion of technical
                    questions.</p>
                <p>Please take this matter up with Foreign Office immediately and telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d520-f1" n="51" xml:id="d520-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it transmitted a portion of note No. 7067, May 7, 1930, from the
                    Mexican Minister for Foreign Affairs, <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi></p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d520-f2" n="52" xml:id="d520-f2-content">
                <p>Dated May 16, 5 p.m.; not printed.</p>
            </note>
